><given-names>AT</given-names></name><name><surname>Lewis</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Howell</surname><given-names>RT</given-names></name><name><surname>Langkamer</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Case</surname><given-names>CP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Wear debris from adjacent to fail total hip arthroplasty induces metal specific aberrations in the <italic>in vitro</italic> macronucleus assay</article-title><source>Mutagenesis</source><year>2002</year>(in press)</citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Duesburg</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Rasnick</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Aneuploidy, the somatic mutation that makes cancer a species of its own</article-title><source>Cell Motility Cytoskeleton</source><year>2000</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>81</fpage><lpage>107</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cell Motility Cytoskeleton||47|81||bib13|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Duesberg</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Rauch</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Rasnick</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Hehlmann</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Genetic instability of cancer cells is proportional to their degree of aneuploidy</article-title><source>Proc Nat Acad Sci USA</source><year>1998</year><volume>95</volume><fpage>13692</fpage><lpage>13697</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Proc Nat Acad Sci USA||95|13692||bib14|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gillespie</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Frampton</surname><given-